Job Department/School **Social Work**FT/PT/Temp **Full time**Location **Garden City, N.Y.**

**School of Social Work**

 **JOB SUMMARY:**
The Associate Dean for Academic Affairs provides oversight and leadership for the MSW and BSW programs in academic standards, explicit and implicit curriculum design and implementation, faculty development, academic affairs, and student achievement. This oversight extends to all program options (OMSW, Garden City, Poughkeepsie, Middletown, Hauppauge and NYC). The ADAA supervises the director of the BSW programs, the coordinator of the OMSW program, and the directors of Practicum Education and Student Affairs. The ADAA works in concert with the Center coordinators in the planning of center activities and focus areas. The Associate Dean for Academic Affairs consults with faculty around course assignments, hires and evaluates adjunct faculty, oversees and approves course schedules, and assigns faculty to courses within MSW program. The ADAA will explore areas for SSW growth and development, including flexible learning options, develop collaborations with state and community agencies, and identify and pursue federal training grants.


This role also includes being the director of the MSW Program. While there is a strong relationship of the responsibilities of the MSW Program Director and Associate Dean for Academic Affairs specific responsibilities of the MSW Program Director position entail operationalizing key accreditation standards related to the MSW program’s curriculum processes and objectives, addressing student retention, academic progress, and degree completion. The MSW program director plans orientations for adjunct faculty, plans course scheduling, and monitors the implementation of the curriculum.

**SALARY INFORMATION:**
In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $140,000 \- $170,000\. Adelphi University considers factors such as departmental budgets, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. An annual base salary higher than the range may be warranted in circumstances where a candidate has demonstrable equivalent prior higher education experience at another University.
Adelphi University provides a comprehensive benefit package for faculty and staff employees. For a list of benefits provided to employees, please click here. **REPORTS TO:** Dean of the School of Social Work **RESPONSIBILITIES \& DUTIES:**
Ensures quality and integrity of the MSW, OMSW and BSW programs across all program locations:* Provide leadership and supervision to the Director of Practicum Education, Director of Student Affairs, Coordinator of the OMSW Program, and Director of the BSW Program.
* Oversees the revision and updating of the BSW and MSW Student Handbook and Practicum Education Handbook to assure clear articulation of academic policies and educational processes, and consistency across school and university publications;
* Provide direction and leadership of academic administrators and administrative support staff responding to requests for exception to academic policies, preparing and tracking academic petitions for leaves of absence, withdrawals, late drops, etc. for BSW and MSW program;
* Provide oversight of assessment of students on leaves of absence to determine suitability for the return to the program;
* Work with Director of Practicum Education to address challenges in students’ progress toward foundation and advanced level competence;
* Facilitate communication and problem resolution in addressing academic\-related concerns identified by students and/or their professors;
* Respond to student grievances in accordance with established school and university policies.


Design, implement and maintain systems and procedures for working with students at academic risk:* Oversee implementation of academic standards including development of academic probation contracts;
* Direct academic affairs administrators and administrative support staff in tracking and notification of students with low GPAs, students on probation or at\-risk within the MSW program;
* Oversee processes around allegations of plagiarism and other forms of academic dishonesty and interpret policy and procedures, collect and file forms and evidence of plagiarism, refer egregious or repeat offenders to the Academic Standards Committee, consistent with School and University policies;
* Provide leadership to faculty, academic advisors, and the practicum education department around policies and procedures in the School of Social Work related to academic standards within the BSW and MSW programs;
* Develop and implement protocols to identify academically at\-risk students to promote positive student outcomes.


Curriculum design and implementation for the MSW program at all locations:* Provide leadership in the delivery of a coherent and integrated explicit and implicit curriculum for class and practicum education;
* Consult with Curriculum Committee on curriculum implementation, curriculum renewal, and adjunct faculty development;
* Plan course offerings for all program sites within established time frames and in accordance with policy and procedures provided by the Office of the Provost and University Registrar;
* Consult with faculty around course assignments and assign faculty to classes, collaborating with Center Coordinators and other stakeholders as necessary;
